request:
Review this top to bottom before I build on it. Tear it apart, I want anything that is actually broken, not style.

Commit 8ad9b3e470 (diff trimmed to the part I care about):

fix(project,dawinterchange): four rows of the July register — project opens claiming unsaved changes, and a DAWproject round-trip that loses tracks (#1517)

* test(project): pin that opening a project leaves it clean (audit M-011)

Fails on main. `replaceProjectData` hydrates the arrangement and publishes
`dirty: false` inside one `batchStoreUpdates`, and that helper defers
subscriber notification to the end of the batch — so the composition root's
trackStore -> markDirty subscription runs after the clean metadata was already
written. Every freshly opened or imported project ends up flagged as having
unsaved changes.

The subscription bootstrap wrote inline is extracted to
`initProjectDirtyTracking`, shaped like the adjacent
`initGrooveTemplateDirtyTracking`, so the reproduction installs the real
wiring rather than a restatement of it. Behaviour unchanged by the move.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* fix(project): stop every project open from claiming unsaved changes (audit M-011)

`batchStoreUpdates` defers subscriber notification to the end of the batch.
Both load paths cleared `loading` and published `dirty: false` inside that
batch, so the composition root's dirty subscription ran afterwards, saw a
project that was no longer loading, and marked it dirty — every cold-start
restore, every recent-project open and every import ended with an
unsaved-changes marker on work the user had not touched.

`markDirty` now treats a loading project as not-being-edited, and both call
sites publish the end of the load after the flush: `replaceProjectData`
through `finishProjectLoading`, which already owned that transition, and
`loadProject` by moving its own clear out of the batch.

Also fixes the knock-on in `pickAndImportProjectFile`, whose
`projectStore.value?.dirty` guard forced a full save before every import.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* test(dawinterchange): pin track kind and output routing across a round-trip (M-261, M-262)

Fails on main, three of five rows. The serializer's only kind signal is
contentType, which maps master to "mix" and bus to "audio"; the parser reads
contentType first and never sees a type attribute, so both come back as plain
audio tracks. And when an imported file does carry a master track, the mapper
still routes every other track to the literal id 'master', which is not that
track's id — every track points at an output that does not exist.

Both halves' own unit specs pass today, which is why the defects survived:
each asserts its side of the seam. This drives serialize -> parse -> map.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* fix(dawinterchange): keep bus/master kinds and route imports to the real master (M-261, M-262)

The serializer now writes the channel role it already knew — type="masterChannel"
or type="bus" — alongside contentType, and the parser reads an explicit role
before falling back to contentType. contentType cannot carry the distinction:
a bus is contentType="audio" because that is what flows through it, so reading
it first demoted every exported bus and master to a plain audio track on
re-import.

The importer no longer routes to the literal id 'master'. That id only exists
when this import synthesizes a master; a file that carries its own master gets
whatever id the parser assigned, and every other track was pointing at a track
that does not exist in the imported project.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* test(dawinterchange): pin that an export missing audio says so (audit M-263)

Fails on main. Clips whose buffer is not in the AudioEngine cache are skipped
without a count, a log line or a notification, and serialize as a bare <Clip/>
with no <Audio> child — the destination DAW shows the clip playing silence
while the export reported unqualified success.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* fix(dawinterchange): report the audio a DAWproject export could not bundle (audit M-263)

`exportDawProject` now counts the buffers it skipped and returns the count;
the handler warns with it, in the same words the `.sourdaw` export path
already uses for the same cause. The clips still export — they just carry no
audio, and the user is told how many.

The count has to be local: `buildProjectData` short-circuits its own
`missingBufferCount` to 0 under `includeAudioBuffers: false`, which is how
this path calls it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* chore(dawinterchange,project): lint, spec shape and provenance comments

Records the two judgement calls beside the code they belong to, per owner
policy: markDirty's new dependence on `loading` being cleared (and the
pre-existing abort path that does not clear it), and why the serializer emits
`type="masterChannel"`/`type="bus"` rather than a `<Channel role=…>`.

