Commit af080b550a:

fix(mixer): guard send and solo compensation so AI batches can commit them (#5631)

### 🎯 What does this PR do?
AI batches that change a send level or a track's solo can now commit:
the batch refused both as unguarded compensation, so agent send and solo
changes never landed. Send compensation now answers the divergence check
its expected-level guard already supported, and solo gains an
expected-state guard like mute and rename, so undo restores the prior
value and refuses cleanly if the user changed it since. Other actions
refused the same way are filed separately.

### 🧪 How to test
Open a project where Vocals sends to a Reverb bus. In the AI chat, ask
"set the Vocals send to Reverb to -6 dB" and confirm: the send moves to
-6 dB and an undo entry appears; undo restores the previous level. Ask
"solo Vocals" and confirm: Vocals is soloed; undo unsolos it. Confirm
another send change, move that send by hand, then undo: undo warns that
the project state changed and leaves the send untouched.

### 📌 Related issues & additional notes
Closes #5554

