fix(yeast): derive the groove assignment from subscribed state

React Compiler memoized getYeastGrooveAssignment(processor.id) as a
pure function of the id, so the panel never re-read the groove store
after its first render: an assignment that landed (select a committed
template in the combobox) left the panel showing the straight template
with the rename/delete lifecycle controls never mounting — reproduced
in-page where the same helper call returned the assignment inside one
console.error while the memoized render-time value stayed null.

The derivation now flows through the subscribed groove state: the
panel computes the scoped consumer id (pure) and finds the assignment
in grooveState.assignments, so a store write invalidates the cache by
identity. Unit regression pins the two-phase behavior (straight →
assigned without remount); the companion E2E covers the full
assign/rename/delete lifecycle the defect had blocked.

