Commit 26e554b75b:

fix(toaster): defer kit writes made before device registration

The Toaster panel mounts as soon as the device sits on its track, but the
store record is created only when the audioDevice.loaded registration
fires (the WASM node finishing its async load). A kit-param write landing
in that window reached updateKit with no record to write and was dropped,
while the engine side of the same write was deferred through the loading
placeholder's pendingParams. The Groove-knobs E2E spec worked around the
drop with a nudgeUntil retry.

updateKit now defers such writes into a per-device queue that
registerToasterDevice flushes on top of the registration kit, as a
separate store write so kit-identity persistence records the edit rather
than first sight. Writes arriving after teardown stay refused and never
reach the id's next reload, which rehydrates project truth.

The load-compile-hydration census gains a toasterStore.ts row: the new
doc comment names audioDevice.loaded as the event the queue waits for,
the same kept-mention convention as prepareOfflineToaster.

