Commit c4f7a685f2:

fix(yeast): write processor params key-by-key so no-ops and concurrent edits merge (#3185)

### 🎯 What does this PR do?
Yeast processor commits compared the whole Automerge `params` map with
`JSON.stringify`, which never matches a JS object whose keys are not
already sorted. Every no-op or unrelated rack edit rewrote every
processor’s params, bloating sync and making concurrent edits to
different keys last-writer-wins on the entire map. Params now sync
key-by-key on the existing map so no-op commits keep document heads and
concurrent `rate`/`depth` edits merge.

### 🧪 How to test
In `src/modules/Yeast/stores/__tests__/yeastStoreCollaboration.spec.ts`,
“does not change the document when processor params are logically
unchanged” must keep Automerge heads after a second set of `{ zeta: 1,
alpha: 2 }`. “merges concurrent edits to different params on one
processor” must hydrate `{ rate: 9, depth: 8 }` from both merge
directions. Existing rebase and reorder specs in that file must stay
green.

