Commit f3a0c6e302:

fix(ai-runtime): stop revalidating approval fingerprints mid-batch

confirmPendingChatActions re-derived target fingerprints on every
shouldExecute poll during batch execution, comparing them against the
approval captured at proposal time. The batch's own earlier actions
mutate the very targets the fingerprints cover, so any multi-action
batch touching a fingerprinted target invalidated itself mid-flight
with 'The project changed after this proposal was created' — every
workflow spec that confirms a batch of four or more actions went red
on main (#1860 follow-up gap; drumBusPromptWorkflow lost 12 of 50).

The approval is already fully validated once, against untouched state,
by getApprovalPreflightFailure before execution begins. The in-flight
gate keeps abort and revision authorization: external interference
still cancels the batch because every project mutation moves the
revision heads isConfirmationExecutionAuthorized compares.

