Commit fc40756999:

fix(transport): send loop-region edits to the live native engine (#3107)

### 🎯 What does this PR do?
Loop-region edits during playback now reach the native engine. The
region has exactly one route to the engine — the maps install command,
whose transport_maps_commands always fences SetTransportMaps and
SetLoopRegion into one atomic batch — so a loop edit re-installs the
pair through the existing setEngineTransportMaps repository, integrated
through the current tempo map by the same projection session start uses.
The write carries no playing state, so it structurally cannot roll a
session that start left parked on a declined maps install; it is in fact
the write that replaces that stale pair. All five loop-region writers
participate: toggleLoop, setLoopRegion, setLoopEnabled, the ruler
double-click disable, and the undo restore. Edits while not playing send
nothing — the next play carries the region with the maps. The brace drag
commits once on mouse-up, so there is no per-frame burst; ordering rides
the session queue. The transport-snapshot restore path is deliberately
left out: it rewrites tempo and playing state wholesale and wants its
own semantics.

### 🧪 How to test
pnpm test:run
src/modules/Transport/useCases/transportControls/__tests__/sendLoopRegionToNativeSession.spec.ts
src/modules/AudioEngine/useCases/livePlayback/__tests__/nativeLiveGraphSession.spec.ts
— the new cases: a mid-play toggle installs the edited region without
touching topology or transport, a stopped transport sends nothing, a
parked session gets the fresh pair and stays parked, a burst settles on
the last-issued region, and a rejection surfaces nowhere. On a desktop
build after #3068: play with a loop, drag the brace — the engine wraps
at the new seam on the next pass.

### 🖼️ Screenshots
None.

### 📌 Related tickets & additional notes
Closes #3105

Co-authored-by: José Costa <<email redacted>>

