Commit 961b35ef7f:

fix(crdt): clear undo history on branch switch and drop stale convention notes (#3338)

### 🎯 What does this PR do?
Two of the four hygiene items from #3320. `switchBranch` now clears the
undo history inside its apply step, right after the root document is
swapped: undo entries were recorded against the outgoing branch's
document, so replaying them after a switch would apply an inverse to a
document that is no longer active. `switchArrangement` already does this
on snapshot load; branch switch was the one root swap that did not. The
two convention notes in `docs/07-conventions.md` that asserted install
state (TanStack Query with no call sites; React Hook Form not installed)
were false or drifting and now state the rule only. The two
`nightly.yml` reporter hunks stay out until #2926 closes; #3320 remains
open for them.

### 🧪 How to test
Regression check:
`src/modules/CrdtDocument/useCases/crdtBranching/__tests__/switchBranch.spec.ts`
case `clears undo history when the root document is swapped` fails on
`origin/main` (mock called 0 times) and passes here. Manually: open a
project, make an edit, create a second branch and switch to it, then
press Undo. Expected: nothing is undone and the undo control is
disabled; before this change the previous branch's inverse was applied
to the new branch's document.

