Commit b5c1dfeede (diff trimmed to the part I care about):

fix(dsp): make the Bacteria oversampler a real half-band filter (#801)

* fix(dsp): make the Bacteria oversampler a real half-band filter

bacteria/oversample.rs advertised "half-band polyphase IIR filters" built
from a "5th order elliptic half-band IIR (two all-pass branches)". It had
neither. AllPassSection::process stored the input in the state register:

    let output = self.z1 + (input - self.z1) * self.coeff;
    self.z1 = input;

which is y[n] = a*x[n] + (1-a)*x[n-1] -- a 2-tap FIR with no pole, so no
all-pass property, so no valid polyphase half-band decomposition.

Measured on a 7 kHz tanh drive at 48 kHz (Goertzel alias-to-harmonic
ratio, the probe grinder/oversample.rs already uses):

  no oversampling  0.17319
  2x (before)      0.15679   1.1x better, passband gain 0.425 (-7.4 dB)
  4x (before)      0.07878   2.2x better, passband gain 0.202 (-13.9 dB)
  8x (before)      0.07878   bit-identical to 4x

8x was identical to 4x because downsample never read past index 3: the
samples upsample fabricated for slots 4..8 (buffer[i - 4] * 0.5, admitted
in its own comment) were discarded and stages[2] was dead. The 4x
"improvement" was mostly the signal being crushed 14 dB, not aliasing
being rejected.

Replaced with a cascade of the crate's tested 15-tap Kaiser half-band FIR
(proof::oversample::Oversampler2x), the same route #787 took for Grinder.
No new filter math. One filter instance per stage driven once per sample
of its own input rate -- stage 2 twice per base sample, stage 3 four
times. Giving each phase its own instance (as proof::Oversampler4x does)
makes every stage-2 filter see a base-rate-decimated stream, collapsing
its cutoff back onto stage 1's and compounding passband droop: that
arrangement measured 0.936x at 7 kHz for 4x against 0.959x sequential.

  2x (after)       0.00603   28.7x better, passband gain 0.968
  4x (after)       0.00543   31.9x better, passband gain 0.959
  8x (after)       0.00537   32.2x better, passband gain 0.957

Also fixed in the same file:
- OversamplingChain::new allocated two Vecs; engine.rs rebuilds the chain
  from set_param, so an oversampling automation move allocated on the
  audio thread. Now inline arrays.
- A factor of 3/5/6/7 kept the odd factor with an empty stage vector and
  panicked with an index-out-of-bounds on the first upsample. Factors now
  round down to a supported power of two.
- downsample output runs through flush_denormal.

Group delay is now real and measured (6.5 / 9.75 / 11.375 base samples),
exposed as OversamplingChain::latency_samples and pinned against the
impulse centroid. BacteriaEngine::latency_samples still reports 0 and is
left alone -- it already ignores the 2048-point STFT, so making that
report honest is its own concern.

Refs #716.

