fix(ai): keep restricted clear-solos and dual-VCA prompts rejected (#3279)

### 🎯 What does this PR do?
Nightly Unit 1/4 admitted restricted clear-solos and a dual-VCA unassign
because post-target admission inspected only the split clause, and it
dropped delete track-guitar when a second track named Guitar made that
id look like a name. Restriction and VCA-group checks now read the full
user request; a literal track id wins over a name that is only a token
of that id.

### 🧪 How to test
In the copilot, with a track named Unnamed soloed, ask to clear all
solos all but Unnamed — the request must be refused, not clear every
solo. With Vocals in Drum VCA only, ask to unassign Vocals from Drum VCA
and Vocal VCA — that must be refused. With ids track-guitar and a second
track named Guitar, ask to delete track-guitar — that id is removed, not
refused as ambiguous.

