Commit 8736dea91f:

feat(yeast): wire rack reorder UI and fix its CRDT persistence (#2132)

### 🎯 What does this PR do?

Closes the last two Yeast audit findings plus dead-API residue.

- **Reorder UI**: `YeastPanel.tsx` claimed "add/remove/reorder modules"
with no reorder control, and `reorderYeastProcessor` had zero callers.
Added a shared `ProcessorRackChain` component (Up/Down buttons,
boundary-disabled, `aria-label`ed, non-bubbling) used by all three rack
decks, wired through `reorderYeastProcessor` -> `commitYeastProjection`.
- **CRDT persistence defect (found verifying the round-trip
requirement)**: `yeastAutomergeStorage.ts` decoded/re-encoded the
processor map sorted by id, discarding any order a user set. Fixed
additively: entities gain an optional `order` field, `decodeProcessors`
sorts by it (id tiebreak, also covers legacy documents that never had
one), every mutation writes fresh order values. No schema-version bump —
`order` is purely additive and every read path tolerates its absence;
bumping would only make older builds throw on hydrate/write. Also
removed a matching id-sort in `rebaseProcessors` on the optimistic-write
path.
- **Two-peer concurrent reorder spec**: proves convergence from either
merge direction, permutation completeness, and that a concurrent param
edit on the moved row survives — the id-keyed-map-plus-order design
survives exactly the case the generic Automerge-list reconciler cannot
(`createAutomergeStorage.concurrentReorder.spec.ts`'s accepted
list-reorder limitation).
- **MutationEngine per-beat cadence (defect 2)**: already fixed on this
branch's base, existing coverage confirms it. No change needed.
- **Dead API residue**: removed `MidiRack.setProcessorParam` and
`MidiRack.reorder` (zero callers, superseded by `replaceProjection`).
Renamed `MutationEngine.getTargetValues` to `__getTargetValuesForTest`
and fixed its stale "for UI display" doc comment — no production
consumer; kept, not deleted, since the spec suite uses it to observe the
walk's internal state directly.
- **MutationEngine targets 2-4**: `octave_bias` and `probability_offset`
were written by the walk but never read. Implemented both, keyed by
`noteInstanceId` (pitch-composite fallback only when absent) to
correlate a Note On's shift/drop decision with its Note Off — same
convention as GrooveModule/ChordGenerator/Harmonizer/ChordMemory.
`gate_mul` is removed rather than implemented: live and offline
rendering populate `durationSamples` asymmetrically, so a duration-scale
would behave inconsistently between render paths.

Known, out of scope: `StepPatternEditor`'s `currentStep` prop is still
hardcoded to 0 (unwired to playback position).

This reorder affordance ships a new user-facing mutation into the
module-wide undo gap tracked at #2111 (`commitYeastProjection` writes
the store directly; no `AppAction` is registered for Yeast, so Ctrl+Z
does not know about a reorder). Not fixed here; #2111 already owns it
and every sibling Yeast mutation shares the same gap.

### 🧪 How to test

- `pnpm test:run
src/modules/Yeast/useCases/__tests__/reorderYeastProcessor.spec.ts`
- `pnpm test:run
src/modules/Yeast/presentations/views/__tests__/YeastPanel.spec.tsx`
- `pnpm test:run
src/modules/Yeast/stores/__tests__/yeastStoreCollaboration.spec.ts`
- `pnpm test:run src/modules/Yeast/workers/__tests__/MidiRack.spec.ts`
- `pnpm test:run
src/modules/Yeast/workers/processors/__tests__/MutationEngine.spec.ts`
- Manually: open a project with 2+ Yeast processors, use the Up/Down
buttons in any deck, reload the app, confirm order survived.

### 🖼️ Screenshots

N/A (control affordance is two glyph buttons, `↑`/`↓`, alongside the
existing expand caret; no visual redesign).

### 📌 Related tickets & additional notes

Filed as a follow-up rather than fixed here: #2140 — `rebaseProcessors`
is blind to a pure reorder (no per-id field diff, only position changes)
landing concurrently with a remote hydrate; narrower race in the
optimistic-write path, separate design work.

