fix(transport): anchor playback after browser readiness (#5729)

### 🎯 What does this PR do?
Keep the requested musical position while browser instruments prepare,
then start audio and MIDI from one admitted audio-clock anchor. This
preserves the first attack, keeps pending gestures and recording
aligned, and prevents delayed readiness from reviving playback after
Stop or a project switch. Chromium first-sample acceptance and
independent review remain pending.

### 🧪 How to test
Open a session with an audio clip that has a clear attack and a MIDI
track using a Yeast instrument. Start playback at a clip boundary,
midway through a clip, and near a loop seam; the first sound should
match the corresponding WAV export without a shortened attack or extra
note. Press Play then Stop while the instrument is preparing, and repeat
while switching projects; no delayed sound should appear. Record from
Stop with pre-roll, then compare the recorded first note and take
placement with the audible start. During preparation, move an automated
control or play a MIDI note across a tempo change; its recorded position
should stay at the requested start until playback begins.

### 📌 Related issues & additional notes
None.

