Commit 03be33ee26:

fix(transport): anchor recordings to explicit beats and unwedge stale scheduler ticks

Recording anchored on `transportStore.playheadPosition`, which is written on
discrete events only (start, stop, pause, seek). During playback it holds the
beat playback *started* at, so punch-in opened its clip at the playback start,
punch-out and mid-play stop closed takes back at (or before) their own start,
and Record engaged while rolling anchored in the past.

`startRecording`/`stopRecording` now take an optional explicit beat and default
to the store playhead for stationary callers. Punch anchors on `punchInBeat` /
`punchOutBeat` (DAW convention: the region governs both ends, not the tick that
happened to overshoot it); the manual paths pass `playheadPositionRef.current`
while rolling.

Also here:

- a retired scheduler `tick` closure bails on its own generation before it can
  claim `tickInFlight` — a flag it can never release, which would freeze the
  live session's playhead while the transport still reported playing;
- `scheduleMidiNotes` took the same value as both `fromBeat` and
  `lastScheduledBeat`; the window start is the high-water mark, so it is now one
  parameter;
- `scheduleFrozenTrack` built and connected its source and fade gain before
  discovering the frozen buffer had already played out, stranding a GainNode in
  the graph on every such tick. Timing now resolves first.

