Commit 0ebd8bf295 (diff trimmed to the part I care about):

feat(electron): scaffold the shell and record IPC parity fixtures

Two halves of the migration's entry packet, both additive: nothing in
`src/`, `src-tauri/src/` or `crates/` changes, and the web build is
untouched.

The shell (`electron/`) hosts the existing `dist/` over an `app://sourdaw`
scheme registered privileged before `app.whenReady`. The scheme exists
because the renderer addresses its wasm and worklets as `/wasm/...` and
`/audio/worklets/...` and needs `SharedArrayBuffer`: `file://` gives
neither a path root nor cross-origin isolation. Every response carries
COOP/COEP/CORP and the production CSP from `tauri.conf.json` minus the
Tauri-only `ipc:`/`asset:` schemes. Permissions deny by default and allow
only media, MIDI, MIDI SysEx and speaker selection, for the app origin.

The fixtures (`scripts/ipcFixtures/`) record what a read-only command
subset answers today, produced through Tauri's real invoke pipeline by
`src-tauri/tests/ipc_fixtures.rs`. The test compares on later runs, so a
wire-shape change made without intent fails there rather than in a
renderer that already shipped.

Electron is pinned to 43.4.0: 44 has no stable release, only alphas and
betas, and the issue's fallback applies.

