Commit fbe92a3050:

fix(yeast): wire the arp pattern editor to the running rack

The pattern editor was dead UI. Two StepPatternEditor instances each held a
private useState draft, `Arpeggiator.setPattern` had no production caller, and
the projection carried numbers only — so mode 7 (Pattern) could not be
programmed, and nothing an edit produced persisted or replicated.

The pattern now travels as the `pattern_`-prefixed subset of the processor's
numeric params. That shape is what the Automerge codec, the Worker message
validator and `MidiRack.replaceParams` already accept, so the pattern persists
and replicates without widening any of those contracts — the precedent is
`createYeastRuntimeProjection` flattening groove offsets into
`groove_timing_<index>`. The encoding is sparse: a field equal to the step
default is omitted, which keeps a default pattern to one key and makes a
projection saved before this channel existed decode to the default pattern.

`Arpeggiator.replaceParams` decodes once and applies through the existing
`setPattern`. Both editor surfaces render one `ArpPatternDeck` bound to the
stored pattern, so Build and Lab edit the same thing, and length is clamped to
the range the codec carries.

Also gives the step cells a role, label and keyboard toggle — they were
pointer-only divs with no accessible handle.

