feat(audio-engine): play stored clip controllers on Grand Boule and Levain (#4981)

### 🎯 What does this PR do?
Recorded or imported controller lanes (sustain pedal, mod wheel and
other CC) reached no instrument: browser playback and audio export
scheduled notes only, so a piano part with a sustain lane played dry.
Stored clip controllers now play on the two browser instruments that
honour them, Grand Boule (sustain, sostenuto, una corda) and Levain
(every CC), at their own sample frame. One projection serves live
playback and export: each loop pass and clip start begins from the
controller value in force there (the carry rule split, glue and export
use), and a move is emitted once across the transport loop seam. At one
frame both routes apply note-offs, then controllers, then note-ons, so a
pedal catches the chord struck with it but not the note released there.
A transport loop wrap or follow-action jump into a clip restores each
stored controller to its value at the destination. Stopping, pausing or
locating releases any pedal stored playback left down on that device.
Pitch-bend lanes, Yeast-routed tracks, other instruments, the native
engine, hosted plugins and transport-start chase (#3683) are out of
scope; restoring controllers when a muted track resumes is #4982.

### 🧪 How to test
1. Import a MIDI piano file with a sustain-pedal lane onto Grand Boule
and play it: notes ring while the pedal is down and damp when it lifts.
2. Export the same section as audio: the export sustains the same way,
including a note that ends exactly where the pedal goes down (it damps
in both). 3. Set a transport loop whose start sits inside the clip where
the pedal is up, with a pedal press late in the loop: every pass after
the first starts with the pedal up again. 4. Stop playback while the
pedal lane is down: the piano stops ringing on the next note; a pedal
held live on a different instrument is unaffected. 5. Draw a mod-wheel
(CC1) lane on a Levain clip and play: the dynamics follow the lane.

